{"id": "EUVD-2026-86735", "enisaUuid": "4d3e84fd-2aa0-3a69-8ce0-1b2472ed8445", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nfbdev: vfb: defer cleanup until the last reference\n\nFBIOGETCMAP takes a shallow snapshot of info->cmap and performs the\nusercopy after dropping info->lock. vfb_remove() frees the colormap\nimmediately after unregistering the framebuffer, even when an open file\nstill holds a reference to fb_info. A concurrent driver unbind can\ntherefore free the colormap while the ioctl copies it to userspace.\n\nKASAN reports:\n\n  BUG: KASAN: slab-use-after-free in _copy_to_user\n  Read of size 512 by task poc/125\n\n   _copy_to_user (./include/linux/instrumented.h:129 ./include/linux/uaccess.h:201 lib/usercopy.c:24)\n   fb_cmap_to_user (./include/linux/uaccess.h:230 drivers/video/fbdev/core/fbcmap.c:211)\n   do_fb_ioctl (drivers/video/fbdev/core/fb_chrdev.c:114)\n\n   Allocated by task 1:\n   fb_alloc_cmap_gfp (./include/linux/slab.h:973 ./include/linux/slab.h:1290 drivers/video/fbdev/core/fbcmap.c:108)\n   vfb_probe (drivers/video/fbdev/vfb.c:459)\n\n   Freed by task 124:\n   fb_dealloc_cmap (drivers/video/fbdev/core/fbcmap.c:151)\n   vfb_remove (drivers/video/fbdev/vfb.c:489)\n\nunregister_framebuffer() drops the registration reference, and fbdev calls\nfb_destroy after the last put_fb_info(). Move the registered framebuffer's\ncleanup into an fb_destroy callback so its colormap and screen buffer stay\nalive until all file references have been released.", "datePublished": "2026-09-25T10:22:16", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-19T09:10:08", "baseScore": 0.0, "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/bf49eac7ed11aabd0b9b790c062742a8e4be97c6", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/040ce3950f64a11e9ee5646c8aaa91fd2e29e245", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/ab664e279eb2a68e55895dd115a9488807280f07", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/de5a0eda59fe4b3eacd1a67c992e54766bb6683f", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/86356f13598f59f5acb1754895747dcdaf65a254", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/5ff1effb047e465cde193d7df95988aa1520035e", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/3c91e51a53cf805e551e5dc8149cd0539a6dbb9d", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/a0a34a40ed299c9c7cff6af163a5b883ee9d6d73"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-97604", "GHSA-8fh7-qq2h-xhh6"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.21, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "059f8a2c-76c2-3521-b811-7449d2d02bf4", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "2.6.30"}, {"id": "077c122e-ac57-384b-9245-8c5bc139081a", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.12.111"}, {"id": "540fd5e4-b166-3524-95ad-afb29b9fe38b", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.2.7"}, {"id": "638a1f72-2c97-3280-ac4c-4c8dd3685699", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.3"}, {"id": "669e274a-a11d-3294-9e41-2dfb96b34ca8", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "5e266e2e0e19532c1b8e2e2bff1eb6ccf42e478a <de5a0eda59fe4b3eacd1a67c992e54766bb6683f"}, {"id": "812c9003-92b5-322b-8db8-cd80d26ff1c4", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.1.189"}, {"id": "8e9e96d2-bfd3-3a53-ae18-c1505600b11e", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 5.10.271"}, {"id": "8f9e6c6d-2244-3f26-8c96-a2f8ad4e4aa3", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 0"}, {"id": "a20ae668-c0e0-3ebf-bceb-fdece4d30be2", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.18.53"}, {"id": "aa6cccb4-9849-3a6b-848f-cab32028c554", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.6.158"}, {"id": "ab734fc1-b1e8-382c-9870-26d741675117", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "5e266e2e0e19532c1b8e